# modes

ditto has two modes: default and keycast. press `m` to switch between them.

## default

<!-- NOTE: add gif here -->

default mode displays a full keyboard using your selected layout, size, and standard. pressed keys light up as you type, even when another window is focused.

## keycast

<!-- NOTE: add gif here -->

keycast mode displays pressed keys more clearly, similar to other keycasting software. for better visibility, use a floating terminal and increase its font size.

press `f` to toggle finger color highlighting while in keycast mode.

## controls

| key | action |
| --- | --- |
| `m` | switch between default and keycast mode |
| `v` | toggle between ascii and box-draw rendering |
| `l` | open the layout list |
| `s` | open the size list |
| `d` | open the standard list |
| `c` | toggle the kana or hangeul overlay for jis and ks |
| `?` | toggle key bindings help |
| `h` | toggle the info bar |
| `q` / `esc` | open the quit dialog |
| `ctrl+c` | quit |

